        "nyc-charter:1043(g)"
      ],
      "text_fixture": "20260605008",
      "text": "New York City Department of Sanitation\nNotice of Public Hearing and Opportunity to Comment on Final Rules\nWhat are we adopting? The Department of Sanitation (DSNY) is proposing\nto amend its rules regarding commercial waste to include the\nimplementation schedule for Commercial Waste Zones (CWZs).\nWhat authorizes DSNY to make this rule? Section 753 and Section 1043(g) of the New York\nCity Charter and Title 16-B of the New York City Administrative Code authorize DSNY to make\nthis proposed rule.\nIn 2019, New York City enacted Local Law 199 requiring the establishment of a new\nprogram for the collection of commercial waste. The program, known as the Commercial Waste\nZones (CWZ) program.\n"
    }
